# 10. Common Confusions

## PID vs IP

```text
PID → Process ID
IP  → Network Address
```

Example:

```text
PID = 4756
IP  = 47.120.46.210
```

These are completely different concepts.

---

## PPID vs Remote IP

```text
PPID
 |
 +-- Parent Process ID
```

```text
Remote IP
 |
 +-- Network Destination
```

---

## Command Line vs Remote Address

```text
Command Line
 |
 +-- Executable path + arguments
```

```text
Remote Address
 |
 +-- Network endpoint
```

---

## Static vs Dynamic Analysis

```text
STATIC
 |
 +-- Don't intentionally execute
 +-- Inspect file/code/properties
```

```text
DYNAMIC
 |
 +-- Execute in controlled environment
 +-- Observe behaviour
```

---

## CAPA vs FLOSS

```text
CAPA
 |
 +-- What capabilities does the program appear to have?
```

```text
FLOSS
 |
 +-- What strings can be extracted/recovered?
```

---

## Procmon vs Process Explorer

```text
Process Explorer
 |
 +-- Process investigation
```

```text
Procmon
 |
 +-- System activity monitoring
```

---

## Hash vs Verdict

```text
Hash
 |
 +-- File identifier/fingerprint
```

Not:

```text
Hash
 |
 +-- Proof that file is malicious
```

---

## Indicator vs Proof

An IP address, suspicious import, filename, or CAPA capability is an **indicator**.

It should be correlated with other evidence before reaching a conclusion.

